{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/SwiftUIAndUIKitEquivalents"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Recipes","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/SwiftUIAndUIKitEquivalents"],"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","title":"Getting Started with UIKit"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the UIKit counterpart to "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView\/bind(to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to keep it in sync with a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import UIKit","import ScreenStates","","final class ArticlesViewController: UIViewController {","    private let store = ScreenStateStore<[Article]>()","    private lazy var container = ScreenStateContainerView<[Article]>(onRetry: { [weak self] in","        Task { await self?.reload() }","    }) { articles in","        let list = ArticleListView(articles: articles) \/\/ any UIView you build from `articles`","        return list","    }","","    override func viewDidLoad() {","        super.viewDidLoad()","        container.translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false","        view.addSubview(container)","        NSLayoutConstraint.activate([","            container.topAnchor.constraint(equalTo: view.topAnchor),","            container.bottomAnchor.constraint(equalTo: view.bottomAnchor),","            container.leadingAnchor.constraint(equalTo: view.leadingAnchor),","            container.trailingAnchor.constraint(equalTo: view.trailingAnchor)","        ])","        container.bind(to: store) \/\/ keeps container.state in sync with store.state","","        Task { await reload() }","    }","","    private func reload() async {","        await store.loadCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bind(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withObservationTracking"},{"type":"text","text":" under the hood — the same Observation framework mechanism SwiftUI itself relies on — so the container re-renders automatically whenever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" changes, with no Combine or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NotificationCenter"},{"type":"text","text":" involved. Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bind(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" again with a different store (e.g. reusing a container across cells) immediately reflects the new store and stops reacting to the previous one."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftUI view can just read "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" directly — any property access inside its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" is tracked automatically. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" has no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" to do that in, so it reports both through "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerViewDelegate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["container.delegate = self \/\/ conform to ScreenStateContainerViewDelegate","","func screenStateContainerViewDidUpdateIsRefreshing(_ isRefreshing: Bool) {","    refreshSpinner.isHidden = !isRefreshing","}","","func screenStateContainerViewDidUpdateRefreshError(_ error: Error?) {","    guard let error else { return }","    showToast(error.localizedDescription)","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both methods have empty default implementations, so a conformer only needs whichever one it actually cares about. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" already